  "title": "Network of autoscopic hallucinations elicited by intracerebral stimulation of periventricular nodular heterotopia: SEEG during 43 Hz and single-pulse stimulation (1 patient)",
  "description": "Stereo-EEG recordings from one patient with drug-resistant epilepsy and a right posterior temporal periventricular nodular heterotopia (PVNH). The dataset includes 43 Hz high-frequency stimulation of the PVNH, which elicited autoscopic hallucinations, and single-pulse electrical stimulation recordings used to map effective connectivity. It is accompanied by contact coordinates, a defaced T1 image, and event markers describing stimulation parameters and clinical responses.",
  "methods_description": "SEEG was recorded at 4096 Hz from 148 channels (131 SEEG contacts, DC inputs, trigger and monitor channels) with 16 depth electrodes. Stimulation of PVNH contacts D08-D09 was delivered at 43 Hz with alternating polarity pulses at 0.25-0.6 mA, plus single-pulse stimulation. AnyWave ADES float32 data were converted to BrainVision without signal modification.",
